qmd 2.5.3: exact in-memory vector scan for long-running servers

A vec0 KNN query reads every stored vector out of SQLite pages; on a
large index that read dominates a search. `qmd mcp` (stdio and HTTP)
now loads the vectors once into a SharedArrayBuffer and scans it with
a pool of worker threads, using the same cosine distance, so results
do not change. A collection-scoped search masks other collections out
before the top k is taken, so a small collection is not crowded out of
its own results by a large one.

vec0 stays the storage of record. Before each search the server checks
PRAGMA data_version (other connections' commits) and total_changes()
(its own); on a change it compares a fingerprint of content_vectors and
the active documents with the one the matrix was loaded at. A stale or
missing matrix sends the search to vec0 and starts a background
reload, so a `qmd embed` or `qmd update` run by another process is
never answered from old vectors. QMD_VEC_SCAN=vec0 disables the
matrix; QMD_VEC_SCAN_THREADS sets the pool size (default
min(16, CPUs)). If the matrix cannot be allocated, search stays on
vec0 and logs why.

Applies on top of 0001 to the published package (dist/) with
`patch -p1` from the package root.

